# Changes to CI and automation request the owner's review.
#
# Workflows and the composite actions they run decide what executes with the repository's secrets
# and which checks gate a merge. On its own this file only REQUESTS a review, and GitHub never
# requests one from a pull request's own author, so PRs opened under the owner's account get none.
# Blocking needs the branch-protection setting "Require review from Code Owners", a separate
# repository decision.
/.github/workflows/ @gitchrisqueen
/.github/actions/ @gitchrisqueen
/.github/CODEOWNERS @gitchrisqueen
/.github/dependabot.yml @gitchrisqueen

# The prompt A/B decision rule: which graders must stay non-inferior, the bootstrap, and how a
# suite is judged. The rule runs from the PR's own code, so a PR could relax it and weaken a
# prompt in the same change. Same limits as above: this only requests a review, and never on a
# PR opened under the owner's own account.
/src/cqc_cpcc/model_eval/suites/base.py @gitchrisqueen
/src/cqc_cpcc/model_eval/prompt_automation.py @gitchrisqueen
/src/cqc_cpcc/model_eval/gates.py @gitchrisqueen
/src/cqc_cpcc/config/model_policy.json @gitchrisqueen
